{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-57237",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $2$ is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\\,÷\\,2=\\frac{6}{7}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{6\\times 1}{7\\times 2}=\\frac{6}{14}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify our result by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{14}=\\frac{6÷2}{14÷2}=\\frac{3}{7}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
